ealth checks, rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed, it failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left regions on mixed versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second attempt finished. All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (note that the RC was unhealthy in staging before it was promoted) and look into the orchestrator error that halted the rollout."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. I'll check whether it was created anyway before retrying, so the on-call engineer doesn't get paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CgagcWtXrr3rVAQgxedVTp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and passing health checks. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. The latest release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0, so I rolled back to it.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished in all regions.\n- The error rate is now about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The incident request timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't open a second one or page the on-call engineer twice.\n- It describes the failure and the rollback, and lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was already unhealthy in staging before it was released to production.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}